OL,3,GNEWSAHow BMX riding 'changed
OL,4,Aeverything' for autistic teen
OL,5,
OL,6,FA teenage BMX rider from Rotherham who
OL,7,Fstruggled to find kit that fitted her
OL,8,Fhas launched an "inclusive" bike
OL,9,Fclothing range.
OL,11,FJessie, 16, who was diagnosed as
OL,12,Fautistic at an early age, said she took
OL,13,Fup BMX riding to help her "regulate"
OL,14,Fafter struggling in school.
OL,16,FShe enjoyed huge success in the sport,
OL,17,Fwinning local and national events, but
OL,18,Ffound most BMX clothing was not
OL,19,F"designed for female bodies" - so
OL,20,Flaunched her Steel and Spice range.
OL,23,APub: 21-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
